CORE
struct_widening1.sv

^\[main\.p1\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p2\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p3\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p4\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p5\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p6\] .*: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Assigning a narrower part-select to a packed struct zero-extends it, also
when the conversion to the struct takes the bits from the part-select's
source; and conversions between packed aggregates.
